@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+---
+tier: spec
+created: 2026-09-20
+status: active
+owner: node
+branch: HEAD
+touches: [src/flask/app.py, src/flask/ctx.py, tests/test_appctx.py, tests/test_reqctx.py]
+---
+
+# teardown-error-collection
+
+## Why
+An exception from a teardown callback currently prevents later teardown work,
+and an application teardown error can leave the context-local state active.
+
+## What
+- Continue through every registered request and application-context teardown
+  callback and their tearing-down signals after callback failures.
+- Raise teardown failures only after cleanup and context restoration finish.
+- Preserve all collected failures as an exception group when the Python runtime
+  supports exception groups; otherwise preserve the first failure.
+- Non-goal: change callback order, their ``exc`` argument, or signal receiver
+  ordering.
+
+## How
+Use one Flask helper to run an ordered teardown sequence while collecting
+exceptions, and use it from both public teardown methods. AppContext.pop keeps
+request cleanup, application cleanup, token reset, and the popped signal in a
+completion path before re-raising collected failures.
+
+## Impact
+- Request contexts and application contexts both enter through AppContext.pop;
+  test clients, CLI contexts, and manual ``with`` blocks therefore share this
+  path.
+- Blueprint teardown functions are included by do_teardown_request's existing
+  blueprint-to-application ordering. No data, permission, or external service
+  boundary is involved.
+- Flask subclasses can override the public teardown methods, so the context
+  continues to invoke those methods without a new internal calling convention.
+
+## Acceptance
+- [x] All request and app-context callbacks continue after failures, and both tearing-down signals run — test: `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_appctx.py -q`
+- [x] Multiple teardown callback errors retain their identities in an exception group on supported Python versions — test: `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_appctx.py -q`
+- [x] An error leaving teardown has already restored the context-local state — test: `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_appctx.py -q`
+
+## Open questions
+None.
+
+## Decisions
+- teardown-lifecycle: D-17 requires cleanup continuation and deferred teardown
+  error propagation; Python exception groups carry multiple failures where
+  available.
