+---
+# teardown-lifecycle — delta
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+### Requirement: Complete teardown despite failures
+Flask SHALL attempt every registered request teardown callback or application
+context teardown callback in its established order, then send the corresponding
+tearing-down signal, even if one or more earlier teardown callbacks fail.
+
+#### Scenario: Multiple application teardown failures
+- WHEN multiple application-context teardown callbacks raise while a context is
+  popped
+- THEN later callbacks and the appcontext-tearing-down signal still run
+- AND Flask raises the collected teardown failures after cleanup completes.
+
+### Requirement: Restore context state before teardown propagation
+Flask SHALL restore the context-local state before an error collected during
+request or application-context teardown leaves context pop.
+
+#### Scenario: Failed request teardown
+- WHEN a request teardown callback raises while a request context is popped
+- THEN application-context teardown still runs
+- AND the request and application context are no longer active when the error
+  is observed by the caller.
+
+### Requirement: Preserve multiple teardown failures
+On Python versions with exception-group support, Flask SHALL raise the
+collected teardown failures in an exception group. On older supported Python
+versions, Flask MAY raise the first collected teardown failure.
+
+## MODIFIED Requirements
+
+## REMOVED Requirements
